DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI RedisSignalViewerPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) owning the vehicles source (web
useVehicles, loading/empty/error/success) and the per-vehicle redis-signals query (web getRedisSignals
re-keyed on selection, loading/empty/error/success), plus the search / category / auto-refresh / sort
controls and the two-path destructive purge flow (web ConfirmDialog + useToast). All six web sections
render with the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel/TSStatCard/TSBadge/TSButton/TSToggle/
TSEmptyState/TSTableSkeleton/TSPageTitle) and reuse the ported P4 RedisDiagnosticEmptyState surface for
the diagnostic empty/error branch — no hand-rolled glass; an adaptive columnar Grid vs. compact card
list, masked coordinates, sortable headers, and a typed "PURGE ALL" confirmation with an in-flight
spinner. Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; the page is
deep-linkable via the new .redisSignals route (AppRouteParser resolves /redis-signals + admin/devtools
aliases). Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an
executed model harness (44/44), with the Shared.xcframework built GREEN and the page wired into both
app targets (xcodegen, 54 pbxproj refs). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to ONE pre-existing,
out-of-scope sibling error (shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift:88,101 — explicit return in a #Preview
ViewBuilder body), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

